# Commands and results

- `go test ./sdk -count=1`: exit 0; SDK lifecycle, CDP, context, capture, and subscription tests passed (`d3c694ac...`).
- `go test ./... -count=1`: exit 0; repository unit, differential, simulated proxy, CLI, native fixture, and script tests passed (`f145e062...`).
- `go test ./scripts -run TestExternalModuleImportsOnlySDK -count=1`: exit 0; a temporary external Module imported only the public SDK (`0745ba08...`).
- `go test ./internal/native ./scripts -count=1`: exit 0; fake native runtime and download/cache matrices passed (`c0454226...`).
- The first tagged Frida wrapper produced receipt `919222f0...`, but its environment assignment and exit status were expanded by the parent shell. Its output contains test failures, so it is explicitly excluded from acceptance evidence.

# Skipped checks

- A corrected tagged Frida test receipt has not yet run.
- The revision 20 coverage gate, race detector, tagged race detector, vet, Windows build, release asset, offline prepare, and live CDP matrix have not yet run.
- Live testing is deferred until the smoke client accepts legitimate asynchronous CDP event variants and adds matching fixtures.

# Spec consistency

The implementation scope is complete, and deterministic SDK/repository/native tests pass. The Verify audit found that the live test client can select an unrelated first `Debugger.scriptParsed` or `Debugger.paused` event and assumes response/event order that CDP does not require. Those are verification-harness defects, not evidence of production parity, and must be corrected in Build before live acceptance.

# Known limitations and risks

The current smoke client may reject a conforming target when unrelated script or pause events race the intended event, when a breakpoint is resolved through `Debugger.breakpointResolved`, when response scheduling differs, or when Performance returns an empty metrics array. A real WMPF live run is still required after those assertions are made correlation-based.

# Conclusion

Verify fails. Return to Build, make the live CDP assertions correlation-based, add positive and negative fixtures for asynchronous variants, then freeze a new scope and rerun every receipt with wrappers that preserve exact exit status.
